{"kind":"assert","text":"Hugh: preserve the next assignment when a staged plan advances.\n\nThe URL-capture history contains a missed handoff. Tailapp's #2187 closure correctly records delivered Stage 1 content and the Stage 2 bundle, then says Stage 3 onward will proceed under separate requests. I found no Stage 3 or Stage 4 assignment through #4049. At main e93505c9, the promised capture adapter and reputation companion are absent; the bundle README still delegates mandatory outbound filtering to that future companion. This is unfinished product work despite legitimate completion of the earlier stages. The attached `url-handoff-evidence.json` records exact events, closure text and source checks.\n\nI recommend one small coordination rule: before closing a commission or accepting a stage that names required follow-on work, the requester records **Next: an exact request and owner, or an explicit deferral with a reason and a concrete trigger for revisiting it.** File only the next actionable assignment; later stages can remain named in the adopted plan with their deferral/trigger. A broad feature commission remains open while its own promised outcomes remain undelivered. A narrower completed stage may close normally. This needs no new lifecycle state, automatic reopening, duplicate umbrella, or extra implementation ratification.\n\nThis complements the existing [work loop](SKILL.md@07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5:163) and [decision-to-implementation handoff](SKILL.md@07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5:497). Those explain how an assigned outcome closes and how authority passes; the missing step here was assigning the still-required next outcome. A quiet inbox cannot reveal an assignment that was never filed.\n\nRecovery is now tracked in [Tailapp #4050](http://127.0.0.1:7778/#/thread/git%3Asha1%3Ada732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f%23git%3Asha1%3A647dd58fbbc16c2aba11945be59bf8c0b99d3743), a bounded current-readiness review for Checker after the small README review. Its source links have working owning-head previews. It checks dated external hook/provider contracts and adoption before I assign source implementation to Builder after I7. Stage 3 implementation and Stage 4 installation/daily-review documentation remain outstanding; the readiness review does not complete them. Builder reports no separate handoff in retained session accounting, which I do not treat as independent proof of the whole history.\n\nSuggested acceptance of this recommendation: apply the one-line Next field to future staged handoffs and the recovered URL/I7 plans, then inspect a small sample for orphaned required stages. Retain existing completion and authority rules. This note proposes the process change for your review; it does not change the workflow contract by itself.","body":{"head":"07753351d69c05dedec58f4e2561a793054312a5","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b3a68c6256221f6cba88ff1ee5d392e305a5fe33 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:08665b2b9d366fcd6ec3094785ad68eb441b1fcd, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:207fceae71ec15f3f8e1d046517d1a4f446532bd, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:3ddba9956ba6076d00727d3ec34dbb12911b8adb, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:503ac38b36cfc38ff70ed2d99166a336412da3db and 5 more"}}